# Line endings, fixed per type.
#
# The repo grew mixed endings: the same kind of file is CRLF in one folder and LF
# in the next (drive/src/quietroads/data/dialogue_act2.json was CRLF while
# dialogue_act7.json was LF; drive/e2e/*.spec.ts were CRLF while most of
# drive/src is LF). Git stored whatever bytes were there, so every editor and
# every diff had to guess.
#
# Each rule below is the CURRENT MAJORITY for that type, measured with
# `git ls-files` + a byte scan on 2026-11-04 (files with CRLF vs files with LF):
#
#   *.json   90 / 76  -> crlf      *.md     46 / 25  -> crlf
#   *.txt    40 / 22  -> crlf      *.html    2 /  2  -> crlf (247 vs 89 lines)
#   *.mts    12 /  0  -> crlf      *.mjs     1 /  0  -> crlf
#   *.ts     74 / 62  -> lf        *.tsx    35 /  9  -> lf
#   *.js     33 / 25  -> lf        *.css     2 /  1  -> lf  (1 658 vs 436 lines)
#   *.py      5 /  0  -> lf        *.sql     1 /  0  -> lf
#   *.svg     1 /  0  -> lf        dotfiles          -> lf
#
# `text eol=crlf` means the REPOSITORY stores LF and a checkout writes CRLF, so
# a CRLF type is still one canonical blob plus one platform convention; `eol=lf`
# is LF everywhere. `text=auto` is the floor: anything not named here that git
# decides is text gets LF in the repo, and anything it decides is binary is left
# alone.

* text=auto

# ── CRLF in the working tree ────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.json   text eol=crlf
*.md     text eol=crlf
*.txt    text eol=crlf
*.html   text eol=crlf
*.mts    text eol=crlf
*.mjs    text eol=crlf

# ── LF in the working tree ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.ts     text eol=lf
*.tsx    text eol=lf
*.js     text eol=lf
*.css    text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.sql    text eol=lf
*.svg    text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.clinerules   text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
.example      text eol=lf
.gitignore    text eol=lf
*.mdc         text eol=lf

# ── Binary: never touched, never diffed as text ─────────────────────────────
*.png  binary
*.glb  binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
